{{wikipedia|dab=hotbed}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{term|hot}} + {{term|bed}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a low bed of [[earth]] covered with [[glass]], and heated with [[rotting]] [[manure]]; used for the [[germination]] of [[seed]]s and the [[growth]] of [[tender]] [[plant]]s. A hotbed works as a miniature [[hothouse]], i.e. [[greenhouse]].
# {{context|by extension|lang=en}} an [[environment]] that is [[ideal]] for the growth or [[development]] of something, especially of something [[undesirable]]
# An iron platform in a rolling mill, on which hot bars, rails, etc., are laid to cool.

